I know I'm late on this one, but this is one of the "best" features
of DUNIX/Tru64.  As root do

	file /dev/rrz*c

Yep the file command tell you what kind of drive you have where
(assuming
the kernel was built to include it).  Rememeber, in "DEC-speak", cdrom
drives start with "RRD".

If this doen't work, check teh start up record (uerf -Rr 300 | more)
again,
looking for something like "RRD".

If all else fails, shutdown, boot -flag s -file genvmunix.  If uerf
doesn't
find it now, call in the hardware boys.  If it does, doconfig !!


Jack


