There are a variety of systems, all Alphas, that run Digital Unix 4.0D.  What
kind of system do you have?

: The system boots up fine, but when it does, it no longer echo's the boot
: sequence to the screen where the old board did. 
: 
: Usually, most systems (that I have seen anyways) show the drives being
: fsck'd and mounted, other system services starting, etc. In addition,
: after booting up, the system console does not show a "Console Messages"
: text box like it used to.
: 
: Has anyone seen this type of thing before?

Yep.

It usually is seen when the console variable "console" is set to the other
console that you're using.  It sounds like you have a graphics monitor as your
console, so the problem is likely that the "console" console variable is set
to "serial" instead of "graphics".  You may need to connect a serial terminal
to COM1.  Or, there is a "consvar" command on the operating system that might
be able to set that variable while the system is running.

        Stu



