Before worrying about the kernel limits, just increase your shell "soft"
limits -

For instance in a C-Shell,

% unlimit datasize; unlimit stacksize; unlimit addressspace

which will increase the users "soft" limits to the currently configured
kernel's "hard" limits.

If those defaults are too low, you can change the defaults in the
"/etc/sysconfigtab" file and reboot.

