A few thoughts,
1) Your current problem is the command line limit of the shell and
the fact that your wildcard gives too long a line... Open source shells
such as bash or pdksh could be recompiled with bigger limits to suit your
needs.

2) Is there any reason why each file can't be copied as it is created?
since copying files one at a time shouldn't ever cause this problem, should
be safer in the event of a disaster, and shouldn't really be a problem to
implement (use cron).

3) With your current tar method, you could compress the tar file before you
send it, which will make the whole process much quicker(less bits over the
wire).

4) Would nfs or perhaps one of the disk mirror products such as ASCI's remote
shadow product serve you better?

Hope this helps
Adam Price






