Jason,

Try looking for /etc/.AM_is_running (note the . )

When Account Manager is running, it seems to create this 0-byte file as
a flag to the system saying "someone maybe modifying the passwd file".
If the system reboots or crashes while someone is in Account Manager, it
doesn't clean up after itself very well. 

Make sure no one is actually in AM, or doing any password work, and
delete the file if it exists. That might clear things up.

Cheers!

James

