To List:

I am replying to my own message as I have found a very simple work around.

In our case the LD_LIBARY_PATH was required by ESRI software's installation
instructions.

I simply moved the files in the directory specified by LD_LIBRARY_PATH to
/usr/local/lib.  The loader looks for them
there by default.  No problem after that.

e.g.  setenv LD_LIBRARY_PATH /apps/arcexe72/lib

is unecessary if files in /apps/arcexe72/lib exist in /usr/local/lib or
several other areas specified as the default path in the loader manual page.

Thanks for the suggestions.

Richard
