Hi!

I'm having some problems with a program that transfers data between a PC
and a Alpha box running 4.0f. The transfer is done using xmodem over
telnet.

The data gets corrupted in a way where all tabulator characters gets
converted to spaces.

I found out that the stty tabs parameter (Compaq/Digital specific) did
exactly that, and that it's enabled by default on Compaq/Digital Unix.
I can turn it off manually by writing stty -tabs, but somehow it gets
enabled again by the xmodem program (one that I don't have access to
rewrite).

On other unix flavors I've noticed that tabs either doesn't exist, or is
disabled by default, so the problem only occurs with Compaq/Digital Unix
(and actually all versions, I even tried 3.2g).


How do I turn it off permanently in a way that'll make it impossible for
the xmodem program to turn it on ?

I looked in termcap definitions for the used vt (vt220), but it seems
that I can only control tab0-3 and not tabs from there.




