I tried pt earlier on, and it didn't have any effect on tabs.

I looked further into the problem today.
The xmodem program actually changes the terminal environment to "raw
mode" because it needs to send binary data over the telnet connection.
In this change, it also manages to somehow reset the stty settings so
any "stty -tabs" settings are lost unless I've done something that'll
disallow any enabling of tabs.

The people porting the xmodem program say that a system("/usr/bin/stty
-tabs") from inside the program doesn't have any effect.

Since tabs is enabled by default in dunix, and this is non-standard on
other unix flavors, I hoped it was possible to change that behavior
somewhere/somehow.

The problem also occurs only in one direction. From the PC to the Alpha
everything works fine, but from the same session, the system initiates
another transfer from the Alpha to the PC, and it is this transfer that
doesn't work because of tabs being converted to spaces.


l8r/Jspr



