In article <38A9BC6B.34A1602A@cmtkg.com>,
Jose DeLeon  <jdeleon@cmtkg.com> wrote:
>The default max processes for a single user is 64. To change you must
>edit /usr/sys/include/sys/syslimits.h and change CHILD_MAX variable.
>
>Then you will need to rebuild the kernel (doconfig ).

It's a lot easier to add something like this to /etc/sysconfigtab:

proc:
        max-proc-per-user=100

and reboot the system.  You also keep your changes to files in /etc,
so when you upgrade you stand a better change of remembering to
make the change again.


