I didn't trim this at all, and I added comp.unix.osf.osf1 which is the place where
tru64 is currently discussed. (However a move is afoot to rename it to comp.unix.tru64
see news.groups for details and RFD)

I have seen a problem like this caused by an interaction of the powersaving settings
causing the system disk to spin down and a cron job whose purpose is to defrag the
hard-drive each night.
The solution was use dxpower to change the settings on the hard drive and remove the
cron job.
Hope this helps, at least to eliminate one problem, and that
you get some better answers over in comp.unix.osf.osf1
Adam Price






