>at 5.x (the size of a long double is about the only one I can think of that
>might be a problem for Tcl, though) so it may not work for 5.x, but you
>should be ok for 4.0D+.

Code compiled on V5.0 often won't run on V4.0x.  One problem is that stat(2)
changed to use longs instead of ints in a couple places.  The V4.0x version
is in V5.0, so V4.0x code will run fine on V5.0.

V4.0D and V4.0F are both nice, stable releases.  For Open-source where
people can recompile, then V4.0x vs. V5.0x is much less important.

