Essentially the hardware it runs on and the cost of a license.
Tru64 runs on the Alpha Processor.
Solaris runs on Sun hardware.
HPUX runs on HP Hardware.
SCO runs on Intel hardware.
The best way to decide between them is to define a
workload and a budget, find the software that you need
to achieve that specification, and then buy hardware and
an OS to support it.

