In article <38A19792.34650D18@notmyhost.com>,
	Zach Anthony <notme@notmyhost.com> writes:
> By default, CDE on Digital Unix 4.0 runs at 8bits.  This causes color
> mapping problems when using color intensive applications.  I believe I
> need to modify "/usr/dt/config/Xservers" but I'm not sure what needs to
> be in there.
> 
> Any tips?
> 

I use this, in /usr/var/dt/Xservers:

   :0   Local local@console /usr/bin/X11/X :0 -screen 1600x1200 -depth 16

Before you do this...  make sure that your server and card can use the
dimensions and depth you supply:  stop dtlogin, and then login as
root, and start up X as follows:

    # startx -- -screen 1600x1200 -depth 16

(use "800x600", "1024x768", "1152x864", "1280x1024", and "1600x1200"
for your screen resolution, and numbers like 8, 16, 24, 32 for your
pixel depth).  When you find the appropriate values for your setup,
engrave them in stone in the /usr/var/dt/Xservers file.  Make sure you
first comment the default entry, in case your system configuration
changes and you need to get back to the default.

