I'm in the process of trying to do this myself.  I think you need
LSM (Logical Storage Manager) to do s/w mirror.  It is included in
the Tru64 install, but the mirror and GUI features are not available
unless you buy a LSM license.  Either drives or partitions can be
mirrored, but there is a special command to mirror the root and swap
partitions (volrootmir).

There is an interesting "clone" feature in AdvFS that seems to "mirror"
only what is changed in the partition.  But again, the GUI interface
to AdvFS requires a license.

Hope everything I said is correct.  I'm still trying to figure out all
the details.

