Thanks for that.   Actually, I think I'll be OK with my alignment since the
application has all its data explicitly padded so that it lies on natural
boundaries.

Where I'm expecting the real trouble is where bit-fields have been used:
the Alpha compiler puts the first bit-field it finds at the least
significant end of the word, whereas the HP-UX puts it at the most
significant end.  So any assumptions about the layout of bitfield go
horribly wrong!  It's expecially horrible where unions are involved.

Mike Holland


