Hi Mike - Sending binary data although usually much faster (not in all cases)
is a very limited interface due to the obvious.  Since you have the source code
and have some time, try writing a small interface program that will both encode
and decode the binary data structures into an ASCII stream type message.  This
way you can test the code on both machines without having to rewrite a lot of
the bit masking and/or field manipulations.  Start with as small amount of data
you can for parsing and encoding and then grow from there.

We have done similar parsers when trying to port code/data from DEC to SUN/HP
workstations in the past.  The parsers took much less time that trying to
rewrite large amount of algorithms, YMMV.

Good luck!
-John

neumann@titan.com

