Bud,

Bet the last unix boot message you see is about e.g. fb1, where you expected
e.g. fb0.

When a single card system is upgraded to dual, the first video card fb0 is
not addressed in the same way on the turbochannel any longer.

Boot using the genvmunix (you did keep it handy for just this purpose!)
kernel instead of your previous kernel.  Then run sizer to get the hardware
controller specifics to be added to the configuration file.

Run doconfig, edit the configuration file with the proper info for each
controller, and rebuild the kernel.  Move and boot the new kernel.  Good
luck!

JET

