Couple of things you'll need to do:

As root, run dxkerneltuner and increase:

vm-maxvas (under the vm subsystem)

per-proc-data-size, max-per-proc-data-size, max-per-proc-address-space 
and per-proc-address-space (which are under the proc subsystem)

Then reboot.

Then when running the program ensure the limits are set to "unlimited".  
This is different for different shells.  I think it's unlimit for csh/tcsh 
and limit for sh/ksh/bash. 
